The filing shows that Target's share repurchases declined over the periods covered. In 2024 it deployed $1.0 billion to repurchase shares, and it did not repurchase any shares in 2023. [1] In 2025 the amount was $0.4 billion, compared with $1.0 billion in 2024. [2]

So repurchases resumed in 2024 after a year with none, and then fell in 2025 to a lower level.

The filing describes the program as board-authorized. Target buys shares through open market transactions, accelerated share repurchase arrangements, and other privately negotiated transactions with financial institutions. [3]